---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="About — 4rch3.io">
	<section class="section">
		<div class="container" style="max-width:72ch;">
			<p class="meta mono" style="margin-bottom:0.6rem">
				<span class="prompt"></span>cat about.md <span class="caret"></span>
			</p>
			<h1 style="margin-bottom:1rem">About this portfolio</h1>

			<p class="lead" style="color: var(--text-dim); font-size:1.05rem; margin-bottom:2rem;">
				A continuously deployed engineering portfolio — not a zip file of
				screenshots, but live systems running on a real homelab stack.
			</p>

			<div class="prose">
				<h2>The infrastructure</h2>
				<p>
					This portfolio lives inside the
					<span class="mono" style="color: var(--accent)">clu5t3r</span>
					homelab: a small fleet of machines running Linux, connected
					via a wired and wireless mesh, fronted by a Traefik
					reverse proxy that routes every service to its own
					<span class="mono" style="color: var(--accent-2)">*.4rch3.io</span>
					subdomain.
				</p>

				<p>
					A single deploy script (<code>deploy.sh</code>) manages
					the entire lifecycle — build, configure, and run each
					service with systemd, all over SSH in a single command.
					No Terraform, no Ansible, just Bash and an SSH key.
				</p>

				<h2>The engineering philosophy</h2>
				<p>
					Every project is chosen to demonstrate a specific
					credential — not a toy demo, but a complete,
					end-to-end system that solves a problem someone
					might actually have.
				</p>

				<p>The portfolio is organized around four equally-weighted pillars:</p>

				<ul class="spec-list">
					<li style="--pillar: var(--pillar-cybersecurity);">
						<span style="color: var(--pillar-cybersecurity);">Cybersecurity</span> —
						offensive & defensive research, SIEM/SOAR, honeypots, DFIR toolkits
					</li>
					<li style="--pillar: var(--pillar-ai-ml);">
						<span style="color: var(--pillar-ai-ml);">AI / ML</span> —
						from-scratch agents, RAG, eval harnesses, inference routers
					</li>
					<li style="--pillar: var(--pillar-python);">
						<span style="color: var(--pillar-python);">Python</span> —
						well-engineered applications and data tooling
					</li>
					<li style="--pillar: var(--pillar-rust);">
						<span style="color: var(--pillar-rust);">Rust</span> —
						systems work: zero-copy capture, eBPF, engines, CLIs
					</li>
				</ul>

				<h2>Showcase-readiness</h2>
				<p>A project is portfolio-ready when it has all of:</p>
				<ol>
					<li>A live deployable demo (port or container on the clu5t3r)</li>
					<li>A screenshot or GIF showing the key capability</li>
					<li>A README with architecture diagram + quick start</li>
					<li>~200-word narrative: problem → approach → result</li>
					<li>At least one automated test or verification path</li>
				</ol>

				<h2>The stack</h2>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>Astro</strong> — this site: static, fast, zero JS by default</li>
					<li><strong>Traefik</strong> — reverse proxy + auto TLS</li>
					<li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> — DNS + CDN + WAF</li>
					<li><strong>systemd</strong> — service lifecycle on each node</li>
					<li><strong>SSH + Bash</strong> — deployment pipeline</li>
					<li><strong>Docker</strong> — where isolation is needed</li>
					<li><strong>Forgejo</strong> — self-hosted git</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</Base>